# Configuration Folder
# 
# Purpose: Store application configuration files, environment variables, and settings
# 
# Best Practices:
# - Keep all configuration logic centralized here
# - Use environment variables for sensitive data (API keys, secrets)
# - Create separate config files for different environments (dev, prod, test)
# - Export a single config object that aggregates all settings
# - Never commit .env files - use .env.example as a template
# - Validate required environment variables on application startup
# 
# Example files:
# - config.ts (main configuration)
# - database.config.ts
# - ai.config.ts
# - constants.ts

